{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.ObstructionGenericity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.ObstructionGenericity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Roots","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Set.Finite.Basic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.obstruction_nonvanishing_locus_infinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.obstruction_nonvanishing_locus_infinite","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/ObstructionGenericity.lean#L34-L47","doc":"**Chippable kernel (sorry-free).**  The non-vanishing locus of a\nnonzero polynomial obstruction is infinite (indeed cofinite): over\nan infinite domain, `f.eval q ≠ 0` holds at all but finitely many\n`q`.  Exhibiting a concrete `χ(A) ≠ 0` at a generic `q₀` is\ntherefore an *easy, generic* condition — it cannot by itself be\nequivalent to the uniform hardness statement `P ≠ NP` without\ncollapsing the claimed equivalence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.obstruction_vanishing_locus_finite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.obstruction_vanishing_locus_finite","kind":"theorem","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/ObstructionGenericity.lean#L27-L32","doc":"**Chippable kernel (sorry-free).**  A nonzero polynomial\nobstruction vanishes at only finitely many parameter values.\nGeneric base ring per §7c — no archimedean input. ","signatureChunk":0}]}